# Licensed fonts — repo-wide, all formats, every directory.
#
# studiocartelli.com self-hosts Polymath under a paid OH no Type web
# license (500k monthly page views) that prohibits redistribution. This
# repo is PUBLIC, so a committed font binary would be a license breach.
#
# The /lab site still renders in Polymath: src/styles/global.css
# references the files by URL and the main studiocartelli.com Worker
# serves them. Nothing here needs a local binary to build or deploy.
#
# Deliberately unanchored (**/) rather than scoped to public/fonts/ —
# the previous scoped form would not have caught a font dropped in
# src/, in the repo root, or in a directory nobody has created yet.
#
# To work locally with real Polymath, drop your licensed copies into
# public/fonts/ — they are ignored here and served at /lab/fonts/* by
# the dev server, which is the second src in each @font-face rule.
#
# If you ever need to commit an openly-licensed font (SIL OFL and
# similar), `git add -f` it and note the license in that commit.
**/*.woff
**/*.woff2
**/*.otf
**/*.ttf
**/*.eot
